        {
          "type": "element",
          "name": "h2",
          "props": {
            "class": ""
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Requirements for Valid Reports"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "name": "p",
          "props": {
            "class": ""
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "To qualify for the Bug Bounty program, your report must meet ALL of the following requirements:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "name": "ul",
          "props": {
            "class": ""
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "You must identify the exact file and line number in our GitHub repository where the vulnerability exists"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Your report must be submitted through GitHub Security Advisory on the relevant repository"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "You must include a clear description of the vulnerability and its potential impact"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "You must provide reproducible steps to demonstrate the issue"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "name": "div",
          "props": {
            "class": ""
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "p",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "\n"
                },
                {
                  "type": "element",
                  "name": "strong",
                  "props": {
                    "class": ""
                  },
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Important:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "\n        If you cannot provide the exact line of code in GitHub where the problem exists, your report will not be eligible for the Bug Bounty program. Reports must be submitted through GitHub Security Advisory only. Payments are handled via Algora.io; please create an account there so we can pay you directly on the platform.\n      "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "name": "h2",
          "props": {
            "class": ""
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Response Time and Respect"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "name": "p",
          "props": {
            "class": ""
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We are friendly and we do pay for valid reports, but we cannot work with people who do not respect our time. Please keep communication calm and follow this program."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "name": "ul",
          "props": {
            "class": ""
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "We respond to security reports and breaches within 24-72 hours."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Do not spam us. More than three emails in a single day is considered spam and will be blocked."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "We do not pay for reports that ignore these rules or are spam."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Only in-scope reports that follow this bug bounty program are accepted; anything else may be blocked."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Do not ask for status updates such as \"have you checked?\" or similar questions. Once we confirm we received your report, that is enough. After that, there is still significant work to do, and preparing a pull request can take several days."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "name": "div",
          "props": {
            "class": ""
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "p",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "\n"
                },
                {
                  "type": "element",
                  "name": "strong",
                  "props": {
                    "class": ""
                  },
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Important:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "\n        Capgo is a tiny bootstrapped company, so our bounty amounts are lower than large-company programs. Reports without a clear exploit path are paid up to $30 max. Exploits with real, reproducible impact on Capgo are paid up to $300 max. We accept and review security reports for Capgo plugins, but paid bounties for plugin code are limited to @capgo/capacitor-updater. Other Capgo plugins are free to use and are not part of our paid product offering, so reports for them are reviewed but unpaid. Payments are issued only after we have identified the issue, released the fix, and you have verified post-release that the fix works for you. Opening or linking a pull request alone does not qualify for payment. This process usually takes a few days to a few weeks depending on severity and release cadence. Please do not send messages like \"to get paid\"; payment happens only once the release is live and you've tested and validated the fix.\n      "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "name": "h2",
          "props": {
            "class": ""
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "How to Report"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "name": "ol",
          "props": {
            "class": ""
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Navigate to the relevant repository on GitHub"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Click on the \"Security\" tab"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Click \"Report a vulnerability\" to create a new security advisory"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Include the exact file path and line number(s) where the vulnerability exists"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Provide detailed steps to reproduce the issue and explain the security impact"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "name": "h2",
          "props": {
            "class": ""
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Out of Scope"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "name": "ul",
          "props": {
            "class": ""
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Reports without exact code line references in GitHub"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Reports not submitted through GitHub Security Advisory"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Theoretical vulnerabilities without proof of concept"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Bugs in third-party platforms, dependencies, or services that Capgo cannot fix directly (report those upstream, for example to Supabase)."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Social engineering or phishing attempts"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Denial of service attacks"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "SSRF or DNS spoofing reports against webhooks or website preview. These features run on serverless infrastructure and cannot be used to reach private Capgo infrastructure, so they are not exploitable in our environment."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "User-owned application code or project configuration that Capgo does not own, ship, or control, including files such as capacitor.config.ts, config.capacitor.ts, app source code, and environment-specific settings."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Access to Capgo bundle files or proof that bundle files can be downloaded. Bundle files are public web assets, users are informed of this, and access to them is not considered a data breach."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Unauthenticated Capgo plugin/API endpoints that are intentionally public by design \u2014 including channel_self set and update/stats endpoints that do not require an API key \u2014 are not vulnerabilities. Do not report them as such."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "name": "li",
              "props": {
                "class": ""
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Uploader or UI incorrectly labeling encryption for bundles served via external_url is not a Capgo vulnerability (encryption of externally hosted bundles is outside Capgo\u2019s control)."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "name": "h2",
          "props": {
            "class": ""
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Supabase and Third-Party Services"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "name": "p",
          "props": {
            "class": ""
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If the root cause is a Supabase platform or service bug, report it to Supabase, not Capgo. If the vulnerable logic, SQL, RPC, RLS policy, Edge Function, or configuration was created or chosen by Capgo and we can fix it in our project, it is in scope even when Supabase serves the endpoint. For findings about Supabase behavior itself, include a reproducible case and the exact Supabase setting or config change that prevents it in a project configured like ours."
